{"clock":1,"nonce":"74bb5fee6a0f730925a8a1ce9878ce16","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793180030,"data":{"body":"Small follow-ups from the project's cycle M1 (`[cycle] steps`, landed from `project-cycle`, head 09b0920). The final review left them as minors; none blocks. Each one is fixed, gets its own issue, or is dropped with a reason written here.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] **Old tabs get a 400.** `stepOf` (`internal/server/issues.go`) refuses a tab opened before the upgrade: it sends step `0` while the cycle loads, and `7` on a `[cycle.signoffs]` project, where `verify` is dropped. Read `0` as no step, and a legacy number whose id the list lacks as `\"\"` (the comment sits in the running segment). Keep the 400 for a string id.\n- [ ] **A refusal vanishes when a comment lands.** A refusal on the step's card (Mark ready for review naming the red check, a 409 on the criteria) is cleared by the next thread re-read: `useCycle`'s `load` clears `error`, and its watch getter returns a new array on every re-read (`web/src/usecycle.ts`). Same on main before M1.\n- [ ] **The name before the list's first step.** With `steps = [\"code\", \"review\"]`, a ready issue's Work row reads \"Plan\": `Name` stays the kind's when `At` is `\"\"` (the M1 plan's interface, pinned by `TestComputeOfAndName`). An agent started at backlog on that list reads \"step 0 of 2: Intent\".\n- [ ] **The rail marks sign-offs done by position.** With `review, qa, verify` at `ready-for-validation`, `at` is `verify`, so `qa` shows done before its status is reached (`web/src/cycle.ts`). Mark a sign-off done only when its status is past.\n- [ ] **A sign-off key no status names ranks as `verify`** in `at`'s rank fallback (`internal/cycle/cycle.go`): the last such key becomes `at`, and nobody can sign it off from a status. Harmless today; a comment, or a refusal when the file is read.\n- [ ] **Direct API calls write ids the list lacks.** approve-plan, spec-verdict, no-criteria and suggest-risk (`internal/server/cycle.go`) write `plan`, `intent` and `risk` even when those steps aren't listed. Compute never offers them then, so only a direct call gets there.\n- [ ] **Code's locked line on a list without tests** reads \"opens with the test\".\n- [ ] **`?step=` changed on the same issue doesn't reopen the step**: the panel applies it once, when the thread loads. Same on main.\n- [ ] **\"Step 1 · Intent\" shows for a moment before the cycle loads** (the no-cycle fallback). Same on main; GB-38 lists the same flash after a reload.\n","title":"cycle: small follow-ups after the project's list (M1)"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793180030,"data":{"add":["kind:bug","prio:p3","status:backlog","assignee:guilbep"],"remove":null}}]}